#!/usr/bin/env python3
"""Talk to an Epomaker RT100 keyboard over its USB cable.

The plugin runs `omart100ctl daemon` once. The daemon owns the keyboard: it
feeds CPU load and temperature to the screen, keeps the key lights on the
Omarchy theme's window border colour, and runs picture and GIF uploads one at
a time so nothing fights over the device. Every other command talks to the
daemon over a socket and prints JSON.

It uses the keyboard's control interface (USB interface 2) through
/dev/hidraw, so it needs only Python and Pillow, and no root once the udev rule
from the README is installed. Interface 0 carries typing and is never opened.

Usage:
  omart100ctl daemon
  omart100ctl status
  omart100ctl show <file or link> [place]
                                    (picks picture or GIF; GIPHY page links work;
                                     place = {"zoom": 1, "x": 0, "y": 0})
  omart100ctl fetch <file or link>  (checks it and downloads links, for the window's
                                     adjust step; prints {"path", "kind"})
  omart100ctl image <file>          (still picture; GIFs go through `gif`)
  omart100ctl gif <file>
  omart100ctl lights theme          (keys follow the theme's window border)
  omart100ctl lights custom <json>  ({"<led>": "#rrggbb", ...}; missing keys are off)
  omart100ctl lights effect <json>  ({"effect": "breathing", "speed": 0-4,
                                      "brightness": 0-4, "rainbow": true,
                                      "direction": 0-3, "color": "#rrggbb"})
  omart100ctl effects               (the built-in effect names)
  omart100ctl profiles              (saved profiles)
  omart100ctl profile save <name>   (current lights + screen picture or GIF)
  omart100ctl profile apply <id>
  omart100ctl profile delete <id>
  omart100ctl macros                (saved macros and the keys they're on)
  omart100ctl macro save            (one line of JSON on stdin: {"id", "name", "steps": [{"usage", "down", "delay"}],
                                      "timing": "recorded"|"fast", "plays": "once"|"held"|"toggle",
                                      "times": 1-99, "key": {"slot", "fn", "label"} or null})
  omart100ctl macro delete <id>     (puts the key back the way it was)
  omart100ctl keymap                (Fn + key combinations already in use)

The packet formats come from strodgers/epomaker-controller (MIT), and the key
positions from dwaycik/epomaker-rt100 (MIT). Uploads are paced: sent
back-to-back, an RT100 shows "100%" but keeps only part of the picture.
"""

